01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Guernica (Spanish/Basque: Gernika) is a 2016 Spanish-British-American war romance drama film
directed by Koldo Serra, starring James D'Arcy, María Valverde and Jack Davenport.

11
01:15:37,500 --> 01:15:43,500
It is the first feature film made about the 1937 bombing of Guernica.

12
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The film centres on an American journalist (D'Arcy) covering the Spanish Civil War, and the bombing of
Guernica, who falls in love with a censor (Valverde) for the Spanish Republican government.

13
01:29:22,500 --> 01:29:28,500
The journalist's character is loosely based on George Steer, a British reporter who covered the
war and bombing for the UK media, as well as Ernest Hemingway and Robert Capa.

14
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
The film explores themes of journalist, spain, civil
war, based on true story, nostalgic.

15
01:43:07,500 --> 01:43:13,500
The tone is emotional.
